# Android signing key. Losing it means never being able to update the app;
# committing it means anyone can publish as you. Back it up outside the repo.
apps/mobile/credentials/

# Built APKs — artefacts, not source. ~69 MB each, and git history keeps every
# version forever, so they stay out of the repo.
#
# build-output/README.md is the exception: it records each release's version,
# size, hash and signing certificate. That record is what makes a changed
# signing identity detectable in review, rather than at install time on
# someone's phone.
build-output/*
!build-output/README.md

# The web export. Regenerated by `pnpm build:web`; Netlify builds its own.
apps/mobile/web-build/

# Analyzer
services/analyzer/.venv/
